## 17. User Testing Guide (hard required)

Write `docs/user-manual/testing/{{slice_id}}-{{slice_slug}}.md` before marking this slice complete.

The guide must be written for an end user doing browser QA and must include:

- Sandbox URL: read from `docs/larv/07-runtime/sandbox-url.txt`
- Login credentials and roles needed for this slice
- Seeded records the user should see, including at least 10 records per feature or a justified exception
- Step-by-step navigation from login to the screens touched by this slice
- What can be tested now
- What should not be expected yet
- Terminal verification commands run by the AI
- How to reset demo data with `php artisan migrate:fresh --seed` or the Docker equivalent
- How to remove/disable demo seed data before production

Run this verifier before continuing:

```bash
test -s docs/user-manual/testing/{{slice_id}}-{{slice_slug}}.md
test -s docs/user-manual/seed-data.md
grep -qi "Sandbox URL" docs/user-manual/testing/{{slice_id}}-{{slice_slug}}.md
grep -qi "Seeded records" docs/user-manual/testing/{{slice_id}}-{{slice_slug}}.md
grep -qi "migrate:fresh --seed" docs/user-manual/testing/{{slice_id}}-{{slice_slug}}.md
grep -qi "{{slice_id}}" docs/user-manual/seed-data.md
```

## 18. Review Gate

After this slice, read `STATE.yaml.execution.review_mode`.

- If `auto-all`, continue to the next eligible slice after the Definition of Done passes.
- If `manual-slice`, stop here and show the user:
  - Sandbox URL: `$(cat docs/larv/07-runtime/sandbox-url.txt)`
  - Testing guide path: `docs/user-manual/testing/{{slice_id}}-{{slice_slug}}.md`
  - Seed/reset guide path: `docs/user-manual/seed-data.md`
  - Terminal verification commands run for this slice
  - Browser paths or actions from `docs/user-manual/testing/{{slice_id}}-{{slice_slug}}.md`
  - Files changed and tests passed
  Wait for explicit approval before continuing.
- If `manual-adr`, stop only if this slice created or changed ADRs listed in the tracker entry.
- If `manual-phase`, stop only if this slice completes a major feature group or final verification boundary.

